# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# LaTeX build products
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk

# Superseded drafts kept locally for reference
reports/_superseded/

# Cached gradient problems (large pickles, rebuilt on demand)
.cache/
*.pickle

# Generated run outputs.
#
# Summaries, per-context shot counts, per-arm costs, BAI histories, gradients,
# finite-shot results and the grouping-routine sweeps are all kept: together they
# are the auditable record behind every table, and they total a few megabytes.
#
# The three bulky derivatives below are excluded. They are large (the fragment
# standard deviations alone are ~55 MB) and every one of them is regenerated
# exactly by the documented commands, so tracking them would cost a great deal of
# repository size for no reproducibility that the scripts do not already provide.
**/runs/**/*_fragment_sigmas.csv
**/runs/**/*_groups.csv
**/runs/**/*_commutators.jsonl
# Part II design matrices B and C (up to 4 MB each; step3_oracle_ceiling.py
# rewrites them, and the per-case CSVs record everything derived from them).
**/runs/**/*_step3_*_B.npz
**/runs/**/*_step3_*_C.npz

# Handoff note for the next commit, not part of the project
COMMIT_MESSAGE.txt

# Desktop-app delivery folder (duplicates of files already tracked elsewhere)
Claude outputs/

# Accidental duplicate: byte-identical to the current report despite its name
reports/part1_fixed_gradient_measurement_report_original.tex
All in one
